ins the distinct coefficient-derivative terms in its plateau and minimizing applications.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"},{"claim_id":"support.positive_curvature","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Applies the fixed-time estimate on a positive plateau and proves a strictly positive Hessian moment for the limiting solution.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.positive_curvature"},{"claim_id":"support.zero_curvature","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Uses the heat equation and a positive-time density, avoiding division by the vanishing coefficient.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.zero_curvature"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=fixed-time-coercivity&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=fixed-time-coercivity"},{"ref":"sha256:7b07c474e9e4b493474081a793473deb1d5ecae2fdcc29bf9c00dc4caa8bbe8a/papers/short.md/sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/passages/gap-proof","stage":"short","anchor":"gap-proof","content_span":{"start_byte":11094,"end_byte":14855,"start_line":234,"end_line":312},"section_ref":"sha256:7b07c474e9e4b493474081a793473deb1d5ecae2fdcc29bf9c00dc4caa8bbe8a/papers/short.md/sections/8045","section_title":"2. Minimality gives contact; curvature excludes gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.no_bounded_gap","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.no_initial_gap","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.no_termi