,"treatments":[{"claim_id":"scalar.smooth_positive_density","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Develops smoothness from the quotient of moments before differentiating, then transfers the quantitative spatial-moment inequality through local constant replacements at a fixed interior time. Compact-strip stability is a cited input; positivity is asserted only for 0<t<1, and the argument does not transfer third time derivatives or add formal acceptance.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density"},{"claim_id":"support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","kinds":["derivation","explanation"],"rationale":"Derives the continuous-coefficient fixed-time inequality by admissible local constant replacement and common-strip convergence of spatial moments, then applies it after q=t. Minimality is unnecessary for the transfer itself.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=density-consequence&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=density-consequence"},{"ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/passages/contact-and-gap","stage":"expository","anchor":"contact-and-gap","content_span":{"start_byte":25378,"end_byte":33929,"start_line":590,"end_line":792},"section_ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sections/23901","section_title":"5. Why a flat interval cannot minimise","claim_refs":["sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/supp